<title>UK: Scapa says trade satisfactory but stg hurts.</title>
<headline>Scapa says trade satisfactory but stg hurts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>British industrial materials maker Scapa Group Plc said on Thursday trading in the first three months had been satisfactory, but results continued to be hurt by sterling's strength.  </p>
<p>&quot;However, the increased volumes of business created by our strong market positions are helping to mitigate the currency impact,&quot; Scapa said in a brief statement from its annual meeting.</p>
<p>Scope's shares were unchanged at 203p by 1110 GMT.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
